      "message": "feat(drilling): fine boring cycle (G76) with a required shift\n\nFine boring is a new cycle choice on the drilling operation and a new CL\ncycle kind: feed in, dwell, oriented spindle stop, shift off the wall,\nrapid out, shift back at R. The shift is a required part of the choice\n(whole micrometres along X and Y); there is no default.\n\nThe chain makes the shift, so the canned word and the chain cannot\ndisagree. The post engine reads the shift from the chain (ShiftX, ShiftY)\nand refuses the cycle by name for a script that does not declare\nfineBoring, and for a chain with no shift. The Haas post declares it and\nwrites G76 X Y Z R I J P F, one whole block per hole, never Q. The other\n17 shipped posts refuse the cycle by name.\n\nA machine file can state spindle.orientation; false refuses a fine bore\nwith any post. The generator refuses a shift the bar has no room for\n((tool dia. - shank dia.) / 2); the command refuses a zero or oversized\nshift. The verifier reads the three stopped-spindle rapids with the\nstopped bar: the edge zone stays in the cylinder the feed in cut, and the\nshank and holder are still read at the shifted position.\n\nProject file, MCP edit_operation and the drill page's Cycle combo carry\nthe choice and its shift. Programs that do not choose it post\nbyte-identical.\n\nStacked on #2823.\n\nFixes #1479\nFixes #1445\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
